## Context

Child of ticket 1507 (tracker). The author split the work on 2026-11-10: the
Codex part first (ticket 1508), the Pi part by a second raid. Ticket 1508
builds the per-runtime seam in `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py` (a runtime is
a corpus root plus a reader) and the per-runtime reporting; this ticket adds
the Pi reader on that seam. It executes on main after ticket 1508 has merged:
both edit the same script.

Observed on padme, 2026-11-10 (key names only, no transcript content read):
78 `*.jsonl` files under `~/.pi/agent/sessions`, the newest dated 2026-11-01.
Assistant records carry `message.usage` with `input`, `output`, `cacheRead`,
`cacheWrite` and `totalTokens`; a `model_change` record names the model.

Not established: whether `input` already includes `cacheRead` and
`cacheWrite`. Settle it on one transcript before summing.

## Scope

- A reader for Pi sessions on the seam ticket 1508 lands, same definition of
  context length as ticket 1499: the whole prompt of a turn.
- The audit's table and JSON count Pi sessions under their runtime; Pi leaves
  the not-read list.
- An absent or unreadable Pi corpus is reported as could not look, never as
  zero sessions.

Out of scope: a status line or live display on Pi; compaction and missed-run
cost on Pi; ceilings for local models served to Pi (they take the default).

## Test

On a Pi fixture transcript: a session past its model's ceiling is counted
under Pi; a turn outside the window is not counted; an absent Pi corpus is
reported as could not look while the other runtimes are still counted.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The audit counts Pi main sessions beside Claude Code's and Codex's,
  with the whole-prompt definition, and its output names Pi as read
- [ ] An unreadable or absent Pi corpus is reported as could not look, the
  other runtimes still counted
- [ ] Whether Pi's `input` includes its cache fields is answered in the
  reader's docstring, with the transcript evidence
- [ ] `make check` passes
